# Independent P2 review preparation

Preparation only; no P2 spec or quality verdict before explicit source freeze. Read the reviewer template, review brief, approved spec, P2 plan, retained principal preimages and focused unchanged dependencies. Did not read the three moving production files. No tests, execution imports, probes, artifacts representing campaign state, summaries, operational calls or git mutations.

## Authority

Computed SHA-256 of each retained source file and matched `principal-preimages/authority.json`: campaign admission `7e15ed500121b4c85df7a838feab51750e1f476a3e5427b9d1a0b1f0f58a89d9`; production runtime `1a232da79f5ddf0c01e48f39dd94008f6ad3b34ed08af385c3787e4f4555e070`; production provider `6077f0a716fa5d64594f5760d86b00f3b2865b605ca25bf3ab57bed07793b94f`. These are retained bytes, not merely hash claims. Earlier preparation notes describe an older P1 hash and a globally tightened ledger lookup; the present brief's retained final P1 and enrolled-only lookup requirements control.

## Focused checks prepared

- Factory/persistence boundary: retained runtime factory methods start at 817, 841 and 1022. Unchanged runtime calls these before `_complete_role` at runtime.py:3021, 3072 and 3111. `_complete_role` constructs the exact primary call from actual input round/role at 1196, returns an authenticated existing package at 1206-1214, and persists only at 1216. Guard denial must precede this persistence.
- Ledger boundary and legacy compatibility: retained production_provider.py:791-882 holds the existing transition, verified ledger load, duplicate/incomplete refusals, prior totals, content lookup, budget checks, slot construction, original time acquisition and reservation append in that order. Final review must preserve old behavior on absence, including the content-only lookup and time acquisition. Exact persisted-call recovery belongs only to enrolled execution before reservation construction/append.
- Request census: historical_verification.py:418 authenticates every canonical request file before selecting campaign entries; it returns all selected entries without role-prefix filtering. artifacts.py:2620 checks call-derived path and canonical bytes. Content lookup at 2648 allows duplicate entries with identical request content, while exact-entry lookup at 2656 requires precisely one call/request pair. The latter is necessary for enrolled paid calls, but changing the former globally would violate compatibility.
- Verified paid prefix: retained production_provider.py:279 authenticates all reservation/terminal identities, prospective limits, ordinal/receipt continuity and arithmetic, then returns ordered full tuples. `_authenticate_role_invocations_v5` at 427 requires equal-size package/reservation/terminal collections and exact durable call recovery with ordered receipt sequence. P2 must verify the full census/ledger tail before slicing the completed prefix; a slice alone cannot exclude later calls. `artifacts.py:2275` reads current records or authenticates old shapes and raises `RoleLedgerMigrationRequiredV5`; it does not perform migration despite the migration-authority parameter name.
- Settlement: historical_verification.py:2215 calls H1 at 2056, retaining exact immutable launch/config/start, manifest, owner and permitted read-only workspace/mount history authentication. H2 authenticates completed execution closure and requires final successful cleanup with exact owned-resource counts at 2336. Calling H2 per prior round avoids the whole completed-history census's incompatible demand that a partial live repository be fully complete.
- Journal semantics: artifacts.py:3175 authenticates canonical files and delegates predecessor/role-prefix/cleanup ordering to memory.py:1630. That fold requires events to agree with each other, not with the caller's requested campaign/round; the P2 consumer must also check requested identity. Canonical role positions alone do not prove successful predecessors. Full paid package binding and accepted predecessor checks remain necessary before author/critic admission.
- Projection/critic binding: retained production_runtime.py:1416 verifies checkpoint-owned records and archive reconstruction, passes its `repair` argument to authorities and folds scheduling history. Every new call must explicitly pass `repair=False`. artifacts.py:3582 invokes `_validate_experiment_critic_binding` at 3439, which authenticates the full critic artifact and exact record review. P2 additionally must bind that critic to the accepted paid journal package and intersect evaluated records with the contiguous successfully settled prior rounds.

## Review prerequisites and limits

No concrete prerequisite blocker found. Await explicit freeze and the retained final unified diff/report/static evidence through a root follow-up; do not inspect a moving diff. Final review will separately assess compliance and quality against the eight named brief risks, preserving P1 definitions and all old serialized shapes. P3/P4 are intentionally absent. No dynamic coverage is available or authorized; archive preservation and reported scoped Ruff/in-memory compile evidence must be stated at their actual evidence strength. Every introduced typed-state/projection call must use `repair=False`; no operational adapter, capability, clock or nonce belongs in shared immutable facts.
